    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: `membershipTier` becomes `'GOLD'` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create; otherwise the existing BRONZE/SILVER rules apply.\n\nI implemented this with minimal structural impact \u2014 three files, all small and cohesive:\n\n1. **`HouseholdTier.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny stateless helper mirroring the existing `BulkSignup`/`MembershipTier` style. `isGold(owner, repo)` counts how many owners share the owner's `householdId` (reusing the existing `HouseholdId.of`) and returns true at \u22653.\n\n2. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** (GET) & **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** (POST) \u2014 each got a 3-line guard that overrides the mapper-derived tier with `\"GOLD\"` when the household qualifies. Both already had `OwnerRepository` injected, so no new dependencies.\n\n### Why this shape\nThe tier was previously derived in the big `OwnerMapper`/`Owner` machinery. Adding the GOLD rule there would have meant a new field + getter/setter on the large `Owner` entity and changing `MembershipTier.of`'s signature \u2014 each edit paying the full `WMC_other` of a large class, multiplied across ~5 files. Instead I added the behaviour as a self-contained unit and touched only the two small responder classes (each with WMC_other \u2248 0), keeping every changed function at CC \u2264 2 and the file count at 3. The BRONZE/SILVER path is completely untouched \u2014 GOLD simply takes precedence when it applies.",
